  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Canicross 83, founded in 2008, brings together people who practise canicross with their dog as well as the other single-dog disciplines: canicycling, ski-joëring, canitrotte and cani-hiking. The club is affiliated with the Fédération des Sports et Loisirs Canins (FSLC) and organises group training sessions in the Var; it says it has no fenced ground, its training ground being "nature".</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The club's website says you just need to contact it to arrange the place, day and time of a trial; it does not publish a fixed schedule, with news posted on its Facebook page. A "discovery pass" gives newcomers 3 free trial sessions, and the "first licence" offer gives a new member the last 3 months of the season. To join, fill in the club's membership form then take out the licence on the federation platform (courses.ffslc.fr); the season runs from 1 September to 31 August and the licence and membership fee are paid together to the club. The membership fee is not shown on the website. The club also organises the "Canicross en Provence Verte" race in Tourves (16th edition on Sunday 15 March 2026, at the Domaine du Château Lafoux).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: use the discovery pass to try the discipline before committing, and ask the club where and when the next training session takes place.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The club is active in the Var, notably in Provence Verte (annual race in Tourves).</p>
